ingredients:
  - "1 tbsp ghee or oil"
  - "2 cloves garlic, minced"
  - "1 tsp cumin seeds"
  - "1 onion, finely chopped"
  - "A pinch of hing (asafoetida)"
  - "1 tomato, chopped"
  - "Salt to taste"
  - "1/2 tsp red chili powder"
  - "1/4 tsp turmeric powder"
  - "1/2 tsp pav bhaji masala"
  - "1 cup boiled broccoli/cauliflower, chopped"
  - "1/2 cup chopped capsicum"
  - "100g low-fat paneer or pan-fried chicken, crumbled"
  - "Black pepper and chili flakes to taste"
  - "Chopped coriander for garnish"
  - "Kasuri methi"
instructions:
  - "Heat oil in a pan over medium heat. Add minced garlic and cumin seeds. Saute until garlic is fragrant."
  - "Add finely chopped onion and saute until it turns brown."
  - "Add a pinch of hing, followed by chopped tomatoes. Cook until tomatoes are soft and mashed."
  - "Season with salt, red chili powder, turmeric powder, and pav bhaji masala. Mix well."
  - "Add boiled broccoli or cauliflower and chopped capsicum. Stir and cook until tender."
  - "Add crumbled paneer or pan-fried chicken. Season with black pepper and chili flakes."
  - "Sprinkle extra pav bhaji masala for added flavor."
  - "Garnish with chopped coriander and serve hot as a sandwich filling or in a roll."
  - "Optional: Squeeze lemon for a tangy kick."
